{
    "word": "cardsharp",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "af951d01-f403-34b0-a205-28a6eae14b1a",
                "word": "cardsharp",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5ed27603-47c0-4a5a-9cf6-763e2343dd2f",
                        "entry_id": "af951d01-f403-34b0-a205-28a6eae14b1a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cardsharps"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                        "entry_id": "af951d01-f403-34b0-a205-28a6eae14b1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A professional cheater at card games."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81f8add0-d8e3-49ac-980d-79285e19f910",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "One of Tim’s great-grandparents was a cardsharp in the Wild West, and was shot dead during a game."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d623a43-4bee-485d-abae-aa75176d2a42",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "While thus running on, the knavish card-sharp was slowly, and with apparent fairness, cutting the pack, which was prepared by having every card but the honours of each suit cut at the ends, in so slight a degree, however, as not to shorten them enough to be detectible by an ordinary eye, though sufficiently to be felt by a fine and practised finger, which could thus ensure a court-card, while the red cards of the pack (or deck of cards, as they were then commonly called) were deprived of their proper size by a similar process of shaving off the sides, so as to make the turn-up either red or black at will of the player."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72b7731a-2863-46fb-b9c5-3a42218aa3db",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "'Why Moses,' said Satan, 'nor Angels nor sinners / Can live without eating; let's go to our dinners; / Men who play at old sledge cannot both be the winners; / The card-sharps, you know, lose the dimes to beginners; […]'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "625ed402-e654-4285-b2bf-3dbd85a881a0",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "Whenever we used to want to take a rise out o' Bill after, we only had to ax him if he'd seen any more card sharps, and he'd get as mad as a hatter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "276cc38c-5206-4975-b969-992294912964",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "In hilly country sheep will sometimes get lost in small bands. [...] Should they prove unmanageable, refusing to travel, or running off from you, the adroit shepherd will practice against them a \"string game\" quite as effective as that the card sharp plays on the over-confident rustic. Catch the leader, or the whole party of rebels, and tie around one of the hind legs just above the hock joint, a piece of stout string— [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94b3c7e8-6f10-4a52-8118-f3edab2da941",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "The cleverest card[-]sharp we ever saw—outside of good society—was a Greek by country as well as by profession; but all the money he picked up in the by-ways of the sporting world went at the hazard-table, and the poor rogue often wanted a dinner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "376c353c-e2d3-44d4-8774-f94132cd918d",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "You'd been running with a gang of card-sharps when I picked you up, and the police were waiting their chance to gaol you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd9849c8-06f6-42fa-b5ea-e2b6bcce5289",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "When the businessmen quit, there had been two other men eager to take their chairs. The ranchers were somewhat leery about allowing strangers to join their game. They had been suckered in by a slick cardsharp once and had learned a lesson that still galled them whenever they were reminded of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca7df70e-26e6-453b-a029-ba80c158a842",
                                "sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                                "text": "The cardsharp asked, ‘Now who wants to make a bet?’ The wise guy said, ‘I’ll make a bet. You stacked the cards. I’ll bet you twenty bucks you hold three aces.’ The cardsharp said, ‘You’re on, buddy. And you’re dead wrong.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ffbc024-e70b-4fda-904a-51640a7a2580",
                        "source_entry_id": "af951d01-f403-34b0-a205-28a6eae14b1a",
                        "source_sense_id": "a99b6ee4-580d-3336-80bb-db88f3fdbfbc",
                        "source_sense_description": "professional cheater at card games",
                        "target_lang_word": "tricheur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tricheur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4d69752-22d5-3e4f-aff0-6c06f234e2a7",
                                        "entry_id": "ad776d62-923f-3383-ae35-1ace34afc156",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a tendance à tricher."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ba11599-ccd7-41c7-81f2-fa8c3f94a1cb",
                                                "sense_id": "a4d69752-22d5-3e4f-aff0-6c06f234e2a7",
                                                "text": "Je suis loyalement passionnée comme une honnête femme, et il faudrait être manégée, tricheuse et façonnière comme une comédienne de province."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tricheur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "682ac937-a6dd-3452-a5ba-0a6a1000c691",
                                        "entry_id": "1f712d06-e7d7-3f03-96fd-e458c81c6409",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui triche, qui trompe au jeu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f863a7c3-5402-43e8-8158-40c5d75d7eef",
                                                "sense_id": "682ac937-a6dd-3452-a5ba-0a6a1000c691",
                                                "text": "Jeannin était joueur et même tricheur, entraîné à cela par un autre ; et insensiblement ils se mirent à tenir tripot, entendez qu'ils attiraient des inconnus à la table de nuit ; on passait du tarot au baccara pendant que nous dormions, et les étrangers étaient plumés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15d69041-af43-4971-95ac-bbfae6844e2e",
                                                "sense_id": "682ac937-a6dd-3452-a5ba-0a6a1000c691",
                                                "text": "Le dessin datait de ses années d’internat. Je reconnus sa face mince et tricheuse, ses yeux vifs, à fleur de tête. L’artiste lui avait donné un sourire de cruauté maniaque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99a66933-dee4-47f0-bcc5-42c288d849dc",
                                                "sense_id": "682ac937-a6dd-3452-a5ba-0a6a1000c691",
                                                "text": "Certes Don Juan est un tricheur, et même il ne vit que de cela ([…]). Mais une tricherie constante est moins dangereuse que les faiblesses subites d'un honnête homme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "251b1af8-6679-4f52-970d-a8ae3ff94ec1",
